# Roslyn analyzer convention: a `DiagnosticDescriptor` is declared as a PascalCase `private static readonly`
# field (`Rule`, `UnknownProgId` and so on), as in Roslyn's own source and every official template.
# That conflicts with the `s_` convention of the rest of the framework, but `s_rule` would go against what
# everyone in this domain expects. So the rule is turned off for this folder instead of a pragma in every file.
#
# WARNING: this overrides the rule by **name**, so renaming the rule in the root `.editorconfig` silently
# disables this exemption. It happened once on 2026-09-04: `private_static_readonly_fields_s_prefix` was
# renamed to `private_static_fields_s_prefix`, this file did not follow, and the assembly produced
# 38 IDE1006 errors. When you rename the rule in the root file, change this line too.
[*.cs]
dotnet_naming_rule.private_static_fields_s_prefix.severity = none
